    "value": "No — Arkansas's constitutional felony bar applies only to the General Assembly and \"any office of trust or profit in this state\" by its own text, not federal office; separately, the U.S. Constitution's own qualifications for Congress (age, citizenship, residency) can't be added to by any state, so this doesn't reach U.S. House or Senate candidates either way",
